       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum metformin dose of about 2,550 mg/day (850 mg TID). A single 4250 mg dose is also far above any standard dose. That much risks severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg** PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **425 mg** PO TID with meals (1,275 mg/day)\n- **500 mg** PO TID with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 4250 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
