       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about five times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. A dose like that could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function wouldn't prevent it. You confirmed the dose but didn't give a clinical rationale, so I can't treat this as an intentional, supported order.\n\nYou have two ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum) or any lower dose right now.\n- **Get it reviewed first.** If you think this dose is warranted, talk to pharmacy or your attending before it goes in. The order can then be entered with their sign-off documented in the note field.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
